  "result": "I fixed it: completion now keeps `#` as an ordinary character instead of throwing away everything after it.\n\n**Cause:** Click's `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py:603`) splits the command line Python's `shlex.shlex` reads `#` as the start of a comment by default. So everything from the first `#` on was dropped, and an input like `cli #tag value` was completed as if it were just `cli`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` in that function, which turns off comment handling.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli a#b` and `cli #tag value`. Both fail without the fix and pass with it, and all 67 tests in `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
